WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.670
- Hi guys, my name is Mimo

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:03.880
and I'm a co-owner producer here at Tasty.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.680
My background is in pastries.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.160
One of my favorite things
to bake are brownies.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.940
Brownies are so great
because they're fudgy,

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.800
they're rich, they're chocolatey,

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.770
and that sweet place
between a cake and a cookie.

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:17.030
I know we're all busy,

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.520
and you might think you don't
have time to make dessert.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.310
But today I wanna show you how to make

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:24.700
a four-minute, 40-minute
and four-hour brownie.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.210
So let's do this.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:28.350
Our first recipe is really easy

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.790
and comes together just in four minutes.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.990
So first, I'm gonna add my
butter into my chocolate chip

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:37.010
and put this in the microwave
to melt everything together

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:37.930
for 30 seconds.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.470
And now we just patiently wait.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:42.870
And now I'm gonna dump my
melted chocolate into this bowl.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:45.550
Then I'm gonna whisk my sugar and my egg.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.120
This is just one of those recipes.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.390
When you're watching a movie
and you crave a dessert

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.740
but you don't wanna put in the effort.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.700
So you just go and whip it up really fast

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:53.860
with minimal ingredients.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.690
And now I'm gonna sift my cocoa powder.

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:58.840
I like to sifting it because
I want it to be all smooth.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.350
Then we're gonna use a rubber
spatula and mix it in there.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:03.510
I love how shiny it is.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.230
This is definitely gonna be fudgy.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.490
And now for an extra
added chocolate flavor,

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:09.050
we're adding chocolate chips.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:10.590
I picked semisweet chocolate

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.820
because it's the perfect bitterness

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.380
and doesn't add too much
sweetness to the dessert.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.700
Our batters ready.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.830
And now I have this
microwave-safe Pyrex dish.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.130
I've greased it and lined
it with this parchment.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:23.730
And now we're gonna
add the batter into it.

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:27.050
We're gonna use an offset
spatula to smooth it all out.

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.210
That way it's beautiful.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:30.110
If you don't have an offset spatula,

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.040
feel free to use the back of a spoon.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.589
Smoothing it out also helps
you brownie bake evenly.

00:01:34.589 --> 00:01:37.530
I saved a little bit of
chocolate chip to sprinkle on top

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.810
just for a bit aesthetic.

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:41.870
It doesn't hurt to have
more chocolate, so go crazy.

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:44.340
That took about two
minutes to put together.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:46.740
And now we're gonna put it in
the microwave for two minutes.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:48.280
And now we patiently wait.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:50.600
It smells so good, I think
are brownies all ready.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:51.890
I'm gonna cut this in half.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:54.100
But no judgement if you don't
wanna share with anybody,

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.870
you worked hard for four minutes,

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:58.450
so feel free to enjoy all by yourself.

00:01:58.450 --> 00:01:59.880
Look at that.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.670
Look at all that melted
chocolate fudgy the center.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.670
And it's that simple four minutes

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:06.110
and you have a beautiful dessert.

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:07.760
And now let's taste this brownie.

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:11.410
Hmmm, this is so good.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.262
And for something you made four minutes.

00:02:13.262 --> 00:02:14.790
Oh my gosh, I don't think

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:16.520
you have to tell anybody
it was microwaved.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:19.210
You can just tell 'em you
spent hours making this.

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:22.270
This is good, but I'm gonna
show you something even better.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:23.103
So let's go make

00:02:23.103 --> 00:02:24.180
our 40-minute brownie.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.310
This is a pretty standard
recipe with minimal ingredients.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:30.720
First we're gonna sift our
flour and cocoa powder.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.490
I'm also gonna sift our baking powder.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.100
I love sifting the dry ingredients

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.100
because it helps me not over mix my batter

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.970
and it creates a very smooth,

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:39.760
consistent batter for the brownie.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.260
And now we're gonna give this
just a nice little whisk.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:44.650
Then set your bowl aside
and we're gonna start

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:45.520
with the big bowl.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.910
I'm gonna add my eggs and then
now I'm gonna add my sugar

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:50.840
and we will whisk this together.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:51.750
This looks good.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.360
And now I'm gonna slowly
add my hot butter.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.840
The reason you wanna do it slowly

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.460
is you don't wanna scramble your eggs.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.640
This is called tempering

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:01.700
and that is bringing everything
up to temperature slowly.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.430
This is looking beautiful.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.470
And now we're gonna
add our salt into this.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:07.920
The reason I didn't mix my
salt with the dry ingredient

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.240
is 'cause the salt crystals are too big

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.040
and usually get stuck in this sector.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.550
And now we're gonna
add our dry ingredients

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:17.740
and we're gonna use a rubber
spatula to fold it in.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.530
And again we don't wanna over mix.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:22.390
The reason is we're
looking for a fudgy brownie

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.060
and we don't want rubber.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.640
Again, I'm turning my bowl
the opposite direction

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:27.740
as a fold it.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.840
Now we're gonna add our
semisweet chocolate chip.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.280
I like semisweet because
it's a perfect balance

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.360
between sweetness and bitterness.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:36.030
I'm just not a sweet dessert person,

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:37.490
I like the perfect balance.

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:39.223
Our brownie batter looks beautiful.

00:03:39.223 --> 00:03:41.620
And I have an eight-by-eight
baking pan here,

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.300
it's greased and lined with parchment.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.700
Now we're gonna add our
batter into the pan.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:49.130
What I love about this
recipe is it's so fudgy.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:52.650
Again, we're gonna use an
offset spatula, my best friend,

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:53.810
to smooth it all out.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.540
I'd make these brownies if I
want to make something special

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.740
but also feeling lazy at the same time.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.250
So I think it would impress people

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:01.660
but it's not show stopping.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:02.493
This looks good.

00:04:02.493 --> 00:04:03.650
Let's go put in the oven

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:07.370
at 350 degrees for about 25 to 30 minutes.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:08.560
My brownies are done.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.410
I've let mine cool for a little bit.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.810
You are more than welcome
to eat them right away.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.600
But if you wanna get this perfect square,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.890
let it cool and we'll cut beautifully.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.920
This recipe makes nine perfect squares.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.611
Let's see how these look inside.

00:04:21.611 --> 00:04:26.040
Look at that fudgy brownie
with chocolate pockets.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.833
I have my milk, let's try this.

00:04:29.527 --> 00:04:30.600
That's a good brownie.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.720
This one's fudgier than the last brownie.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:35.107
It has a nice chew and it
just melts in your mouth.

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:36.640
This one is really good.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:38.270
But if you're a chocolate lover,

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.700
let's get into the next one.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.830
To get started on our four-hour brownie,

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:43.040
we're gonna brown some butter.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.425
I like to brown my butter in a light pan.

00:04:45.425 --> 00:04:47.900
That way I can see the
milk solids browning.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:49.550
I'm using two sticks of butter

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:52.490
because I want more flavor
in it, I want more fat,

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:53.910
I want it to be decadent.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.380
I want it to show stopping.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.390
When you browning butter,

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:59.300
you always wanna do it on
low heat and constantly stir.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.910
So what you're seeing over
here are the milk solids

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:03.610
and this is what you want to brown.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:05.800
So we want this to sink to the bottom

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:08.529
and that's what's gonna give
you the deeper, nuttier flavor.

00:05:08.529 --> 00:05:11.970
Just don't rush it, take your
time, you don't wanna burn it.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:13.537
Also, like who does wanna take a break

00:05:13.537 --> 00:05:15.658
while they're cooking
and just stir butter.

00:05:15.658 --> 00:05:17.650
As soon as you see the brown bits,

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.910
you wanna quickly remove it from heat

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:21.660
and put it in a different container

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:23.480
because you don't wanna overcook it.

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:25.210
While our brown butter is still hot,

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.910
we're gonna mix it with our sugar

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:29.680
and adding hot butter into
sugar is gonna give your brownie

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.390
the beautiful shiny exterior.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:34.270
In my opinion, this makes
a great dessert right here.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.540
We can just stop now
and call this dessert.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.290
We're gonna set this aside to cool

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:40.530
and we're gonna pull an espresso shot

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:41.920
because we're fancy like that.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.300
I like to add coffee to
my chocolate desserts

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.870
'cause it just helps enhance
the chocolate flavor.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.270
But if you don't have an
espresso machine, don't worry,

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:52.600
because you can add regular
coffee, you can add cold brew,

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:53.780
you can even add stout.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:56.370
It's just a nice way to add
complexity to your dessert.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.910
So I'm gonna show you guys
how I pull my shot at home.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:01.660
I'm gonna add about 15 grams of espresso.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.100
I'm gonna use my knife and brush it off.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:07.390
I'm gonna use this little
guy to push the coffee down.

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:09.360
Now I'm gonna attach this to the machine.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:10.350
Now we pull.

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.780
We're looking for only two ounces.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.770
All right, we got two ounces of espresso.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:15.830
Let's get back to our batter.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:18.050
So next we can add our egg starch sugar.

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:19.360
I like to add it one at a time.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:20.762
That way it's well incorporated.

00:06:20.762 --> 00:06:23.820
So we're gonna make this for
about two to three minutes

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.460
until it gets lighter in color

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:27.760
and this helps us get air into the batter.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:29.693
Next we're gonna add our espresso,

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.540
vegetable oil and vanilla extract.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.240
Our wet ingredients are all ready,

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.260
so now we're gonna sift
our dry ingredients.

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:40.050
Now we're gonna sift together our flour,

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:42.070
cocoa powder, and baking powder.

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:45.310
Again, we sift because we're
gonna break up these lumps.

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:47.620
If you don't have a sifter,
you can just get a whisk

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.050
and whisk everything very well.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:50.290
We can add our salt.

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:52.610
If the time commitment makes you scared,

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:54.400
honestly, just give it a try.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.570
I promise this recipe is not that hard.

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:58.570
Now we're gonna add our dry ingredient

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:01.760
into our wet ingredient
and slowly fold it.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:04.560
And again, I'm turning my
bowl the opposite direction

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:07.620
as a fold in the wet
ingredient into the dry.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:09.790
It's almost mixed but not quite.

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:11.370
And I'm gonna add my chocolate now

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.570
because I wanna stop mixing it

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.080
right when everything is incorporated

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.350
and I don't wanna over mix it.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.810
In this bowl I have a mixture
of semisweet chocolate

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:19.660
and milk chocolate.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.650
And I'm gonna set some
chunks of chocolate aside

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:23.200
because we're gonna use them as garnish.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.410
And I've broken them
up into different sizes

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:27.310
'cause I just want big
chunks of chocolate,

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:28.840
I want little melty chocolate.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.770
So the milk chocolate
is gonna help balance

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:32.450
the bitterness of the dark chocolate.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:36.330
Now I'll add my batter into my
8-by-12 prepared baking pan.

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:39.180
Look at all that chocolate.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:41.360
It was like half upon
the chocolate in here.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.070
Again, we're doing the same thing.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:45.520
Spread it using an offset spatula.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.370
This is a recipe you wanna
make if you wanna feel fancy

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:50.940
and if your friends
love chocolate, like me.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:53.210
Last thing we're gonna do is
garnish it with our chocolate.

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:55.800
I want it to look perfect
and rustic at the same time.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.060
You got to find that balance.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:58.930
And now comes the secret.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:01.880
We are gonna chill this for two hours.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:04.020
And you thought you were
gonna work for four hours,

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:06.530
but there's a lot of
downtime in this recipe.

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:09.480
Chilling it for two hours
helps develop the flavors

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.070
and gives it a shiny top.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:13.340
You can even leave it in the
fridge overnight if you want

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:14.680
but we're not that extra.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.550
All right, I'm gonna go
put this in the fridge

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:19.310
and relax for two hours
and I'll be right back.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:20.143
We're back.

00:08:20.143 --> 00:08:21.500
It's been chilling for two hours.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.290
You can already see the difference.

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:26.190
The batter is more firm,
there's shine into it

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:27.500
so it's ready to be baked.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:32.050
I'm gonna go bake this at 350
for about 35 to 40 minutes.

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:33.500
I know it's been a long time,

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.180
but I promise it's worth the wait.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:37.360
Our four-hour brownies out of the oven.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:39.250
I'd let it cool for almost an hour

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:40.520
and we're at the finish line.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:43.170
But before we cut into it, I
wanna sprinkle some sea salt.

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:46.070
I'm gonna cut this into
eight generous pieces.

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:47.170
I'll start at the middle.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.230
She cuts so beautifully.

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.070
I can hear the crunch on the top

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:53.300
and feel the gooeyness of the middle.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.410
This is a very generous piece

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:57.410
and anyone who spent four hours

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:58.980
making a brownie deserves it.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:01.030
Let's check one of the pieces.

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:02.670
Look at the middle.

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:04.190
It looks perfect.

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.040
It's dense, it's chocolatey.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:07.393
I cannot wait to try it.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:09.970
This is definitely my favorite.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:11.960
The hints of the salt on the top,

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.660
the mixture of the milk chocolate.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:15.930
Everything, it's just perfectly balanced.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:17.660
I definitely recommend leaving it

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:20.310
in the fridge for two hours
because it makes a difference.

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:21.580
All right, that's it.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:24.090
Today we made a four-minute, 40-minute

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:25.700
and a four-hour brownie.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.780
If you have any questions,
leave it in the comment.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:28.980
I love to hear from you.

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:31.370
Just remember, there's
always time for brownies.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:34.330
I hope you like this a choco-lot.

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:35.880
Katie's making me say this.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.051
Bye guys.

00:09:37.051 --> 00:09:40.718
(light bright upbeat music)

